 r"I am writing to apply for the Technology Graduate Programme at Centrica. I completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London in September 2026, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. Across my academic and professional experience I have built data pipelines and machine learning models, and turned them into tools that real users rely on.",

 r"What attracts me most to Centrica is that the technology has a visible end point: the energy and billing services customers use every day, and an energy system that no longer relies on fossil fuels. The programme's three rotations across software, data engineering, data science and cloud are exactly how I would like to grow, by learning how a digital product is built end to end before choosing where to specialise. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, understanding what users actually need, and turning it into a solution that can be tested and improved.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK I analyse merchant and transaction data in SQL and Python and build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. When my supervisor asked me to configure a merchant campaign by hand, I worked out the logic and used Claude Code to build an AI agent with a validation step to check its accuracy. It cut the time the task took by around 40 to 50 percent, and it taught me that automation is only valuable when people can trust its output.",

 r"At DS Digital Technology I worked as a Data Scientist Intern on a patient-facing AI product for a pharmaceutical client. I built a Python pipeline that called six LLM APIs with retrieval augmentation and scored more than 2,400 responses against a 246-question benchmark the client adopted as its acceptance standard, and a second pipeline that turned 4,800 free-text patient threads into structured data. I learned how much good engineering depends on defining what success looks like before writing the code.",

 r"My MSc dissertation applied machine learning to 458,840 UK Biobank participants, comparing logistic regression with three tree ensembles and using causal forests to estimate the effect of lifestyle change, and I delivered the results as an interactive Streamlit app. Earlier, at Westlake University, I refactored and parallelised a research pipeline in Python and R, cutting processing time by around 60 percent. Both taught me to write reproducible, version-controlled code that other people can build on.",

 r"I would bring Centrica strong Python and SQL, hands-on experience across data pipelines, machine learning and AI tools, and the curiosity to learn new areas such as cloud and software engineering quickly. I have the right to work in the UK until January 2029 without sponsorship, and I am based in London and happy to travel or relocate between placements.",

 r"Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my experience in data, machine learning and automation could contribute to Centrica's Technology Graduate Programme.",
